DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The BBUUSS__AADDDD__CCHHIILLDD() method is used by the driver identify routine to add
     devices to the tree.  It can also be used to add children to buses that
     implement this routine in other contexts, although the behavior is bus
     specific.  Please see device_add_child(9) for more details.  The inter‐
     face is the same as device_add_child(9) however, the bus' BBUUSS__AADDDD__CCHHIILLDD()
     is called.

     Buses implementing BBUUSS__AADDDD__CCHHIILLDD() should insert the device into the tree
     using device_add_child(9) before adding things such as their own ivars
     and resource lists to the device.  BBUUSS__AADDDD__CCHHIILLDD() is not called by
     device_add_child(9).  BBUUSS__AADDDD__CCHHIILLDD() instead calls device_add_child(9).

     A panic will result when called for a bus that does not implement
     BBUUSS__AADDDD__CCHHIILLDD().  Some buses require a special bus-specific routine to be
     called instead of BBUUSS__AADDDD__CCHHIILLDD().

